# WhenWorks Bugfix Specs

This file tracks bug specifications for WhenWorks, following the same Spec/*.ospec
convention referenced in CLAUDE.md (architecture.ospec, features.ospec, api-design.ospec).
Each entry documents a reported bug, its root cause, and the agreed fix approach before
implementation begins.

---

## BUG-52: Not all participants showing when deleting an event

### Status
Implemented.

### GitHub Issue
#52

### Summary
When a logged-in user opens the "My Events" page and attempts to delete a participant
they created for an event, the "Delete Participant" dropdown only ever shows one
participant, even if that user created multiple participant records for the same event.

### Reported Behavior
1. Go to "My Events" while logged in.
2. Click the trash icon for an event.
3. Click the "Delete Participant" radio button.
4. Only the user's first participant for that event appears in the dropdown —
   any additional participants they created for the same event are missing.

### Expected Behavior
All participant records that the current user has created for a given event should
appear as options in the "Delete Participant" dropdown, so the user can choose which
one to delete.

### Root Cause
`MyEventsController.Index` (WhenWorksWeb/Controllers/MyEventsController.cs:57-64) loads
at most one participant per event for the current user:

```csharp
ParticipantId = e.Participants
    .Where(p => p.UserId == currentUserId)
    .Select(p => (int?)p.Id)
    .FirstOrDefault(),
ParticipantDisplayName = e.Participants
    .Where(p => p.UserId == currentUserId)
    .Select(p => p.DisplayName)
    .FirstOrDefault() ?? string.Empty
```

`MyEventViewModel` only has singular `ParticipantId` / `ParticipantDisplayName` properties,
and the view (WhenWorksWeb/Views/MyEvents/Index.cshtml) stores that single participant as
`data-participant-id` / `data-participant-display-name` attributes on the event row
(lines 40-42). `openDeleteModal()` in the page script (lines 217-239) then builds the
"Delete Participant" `<select>` from just that one data attribute pair, so any additional
participants the user created for the same event are never surfaced, regardless of how
many actually exist in the database.

### Proposed Fix
- **Data layer**: Change the `MyEventsController.Index` query to project *all* of the
  current user's participants per event (id + display name pairs), not just the first
  one via `FirstOrDefault()`.
- **View model**: Extend `MyEventViewModel` to carry a collection of the user's
  participants for the event (e.g. `IReadOnlyList<(int Id, string DisplayName)>`) instead
  of a single `ParticipantId`/`ParticipantDisplayName` pair.
- **View/JS**: Update `Index.cshtml` to serialize the full participant list onto the event
  row as a `data-participants` attribute, using `System.Text.Json.JsonSerializer.Serialize`
  (not hand-built/concatenated JSON strings) so the value is valid JSON and safely HTML-attribute-encoded
  by Razor regardless of characters in a participant's display name. Update `openDeleteModal()`
  to parse that JSON and populate the `<select>` with one `<option>` per participant instead
  of a single hard-coded option.
- **Controller `Delete` action**: No change expected — it already accepts an explicit
  `participantId` and verifies it belongs to the current user and event
  (MyEventsController.cs:130-152), so it will work correctly once the dropdown offers the
  full set of choices.

### Acceptance Criteria
- A user who has created 2+ participant records tied to their account for the same event
  sees all of them listed in the "Delete Participant" dropdown on the My Events page.
- Selecting any listed participant and confirming deletion removes only that participant
  record (and nulls out its message references, per existing behavior).
- Users with exactly one participant for an event see no change in behavior.
- Users with zero participants for an event still see the "no participant to delete" state.

### Out of Scope
- Any change to how participants are created or associated with users.
- Any change to the "Delete Event" flow.
